    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Lineage distinguishes substrate, development product, source project, release cut, product, install, artifact and product definition. A release cut v<version>-rc.<n> is immutable point-in-time release identity; mutable v<version> is a discovery selector for the highest-ordinal published cut.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1250,
          "quote":"The roles are distinct objects with distinct identities,\nsubstrate, development product, source project, release cut, product,\ninstall, artifact and product definition, defined once in FOUNDATIONS §2\n(product lineage objects) with their governing rules and the compiler\nanalogy; the product definition is the source project's present-tense\nsurface, not the released artifact and not the builder that happens to be\nrunning the build (P3).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F6.%20Lineage%20and%20release",
          "start_line":1244
        },
        {
          "end_line":1259,
          "quote":"The only exact operative release identifier is the immutable release-cut\ntag `v<version>-rc.<n>` (P3). That cut is a\npoint-in-time release identity, a boundary over the feature set accepted\nfor that cut, and part of release metadata and release-process evaluation;\nit is not part of the live project specification. The mutable `v<version>`\ntag is a version-line discovery selector to the highest-ordinal published\nimmutable cut; it is not an exact dependency, evidence or constitutional\nbasis and cannot silently change a consumer selection.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F6.%20Lineage%20and%20release",
