    {
      "applies_to_keys":["method_procedures"],
      "conditions":["A feature is introduced or changed."],
      "exceptions":["Design/implementation/tests may co-evolve only under the applicable conditions stated here."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1128,
          "quote":"When a feature is introduced or changed: update goals if the current\nbounded work wave or overriding concerns have changed; update intent if the\npurpose or scope has changed; update product if the current product\nrealisation, terms, boundaries or end-state shape have changed; update\nrequirements so the invariant truths are explicit as a decomposition of the\nproduct definition, including any lifecycle obligations or named lifecycle\nambiguity gaps, and classify each new or changed requirement by category;\nestablish or update design so it owns the governing structural HOW, where\nunder the design profile its decision-completeness rule applies (design,\nimplementation and tests may co-evolve only when its co-evolution predicate\nholds, otherwise the smallest causally closed affected design set is\naccepted before retained implementation establishes an unresolved,\ncontradictory or materially non-equivalent relation;\n[DESIGN_MODULE](DESIGN_MODULE.md)), and\nwhere that profile does not apply design, implementation and tests may\nco-evolve when upstream truth leaves no unresolved material design\ndecision, and when such a decision remains the affected design is accepted\nbefore retained implementation establishes it, ADRs being one valid design\nform; write scenarios for capability claims that require operational proof\nand define other evidence surfaces for non-capability requirements where\nappropriate; prefer declarative expression of the problem and acceptance\nsurface before adding imperative mechanism;",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FProcedures",
          "start_line":1107
        }
      ],
      "key":"feature_change_procedure",
      "statement":"After triage establishes a supported lawful class and affected span, update goals if wave/overriding concerns change; intent if purpose/scope changes; product if realisation/terms/boundaries/end-state changes; requirements with invariant decomposition, lifecycle obligations/gaps and category for each new/changed requirement; and design with governing structural HOW. Under the design profile, co-evolution requires its predicate, otherwise accept the smallest causally closed affected design set before retained implementation establishes unresolved/contradictory/materially nonequivalent relations. Outside the profile, co-evolution requires no unresolved material design decision; otherwise accept affected design first. ADRs are one design form. Write operational-proof scenarios for applicable capabilities and appropriate other evidence for non-capabilities; prefer declarative problem/acceptance expression. Check every reconstruction boundary, record/govern major ambiguity by declared risk appetite, develop under selected design, reconcile design/code/tests before promotion/closure, and verify reality through events/projection/delta.",
      "uncertainty":"The design profile's co-evolution predicate is not supplied."
